VERSION 5 — security work and boundaries
There is no SQL database, SQL driver or application query endpoint. Search strings are literal text, not evaluated SQL or code. Demo session markers grant no server permissions.
Added shared text escaping, exact-host HTTPS film/poster URL checks, path-traversal rejection, whitelist-based stored-ID/preferences handling and catalogue build validation.
Removed inline error handlers and use delegated JavaScript listeners. Configured a CSP excluding inline/eval scripts and disabling object embedding, base changes and form submission.
Configured no-referrer, nosniff, restricted browser permissions and HSTS headers, with one header definition for preview, Cloudflare static headers and Vercel configuration. Meta CSP also protects application pages.
External navigation uses noopener/noreferrer. Watchlist CSV exports protect formula prefixes. Browser storage errors fall back to visit-only operation.
No absolute-security claim is made. Demo sign-in is not authentication; browser-local preferences are not sensitive account data. A future real-account/backend implementation needs a new security review.

VERSION 5 — validation and corrections
Sixteen model/data/security checks cover complete source coverage, no extra films, unique IDs/URLs, ranking, preferences, storage validation, hostile text, literal SQL-style searches, URL restrictions, CSP directives and removal of source filenames/old controls.
Browser verification covers entry, all demo providers, preferences and consent, saving/reload, conflict handling, exports, clear data, Surprise me, details, search, Gmail target, legal settings and responsive layouts. Additional checks attempt poisoned storage and a blocked inline script.
A unit assertion originally confused JavaScript .onclick property assignments with inline HTML event attributes; the test was corrected to inspect actual inline attributes.
Immediate light-theme screenshots showed intermediate transition colours; settled computed colours confirmed readable white panels/dark type, and final evidence uses a transition wait.
Final browser suite passed at 360, 390, 768, 1024 and 1440 CSS pixels, with no horizontal overflow or normal-flow JavaScript/CSP errors. Poisoned storage and inline-script probes passed. Cross-tab consent removal and completely blocked browser storage also passed.
The local preview connection queue was increased to 128 after observing net::ERR_CONNECTION_RESET on simultaneous module requests; this resolved intermittent browser setup timeouts.
Visual review corrected an inherited bottom offset that pulled entrance cards over the entry button. Opening modals now closes mobile navigation. Removed unused legacy title migration and dotted raster-logo assets from current source.
Source documentation comprises design.md, readme.md, SECURITY.md, VERIFICATION.md and this chronological log. Security review states limits rather than claiming certification.
The exact release source is identified by the final Git commit and native Sites version; the log does not embed its own future commit SHA, avoiding a self-referential change.

